Starting this week, France will charge a penalty on cheaply made clothing sold by ultra-fast fashion retailers, with the fee reaching nearly €20 per item by 2030. Aimed at platforms like Shein, Temu and AliExpress, the levy follows a June law targeting disposable fashion's environmental toll, though rival brands like H&M and Zara are exempt.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b81f0872-a55b-11f1-bfba-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T095850Z-1200926585-RC27HIARHQ0D-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b81f0872-a55b-11f1-bfba-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T095850Z-1200926585-RC27HIARHQ0D-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a3534ae-a554-11f1-b888-bf56321c7dab</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:55:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b81f0872-a55b-11f1-bfba-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T095850Z-1200926585-RC27HIARHQ0D-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg">© Jorge Silva, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Controversial West African activist Kemi Seba detained in Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20241015-controversial-west-african-activist-kemi-seba-detained-in-paris</link><description>
Kemi Seba, a controversial African activist known for his virulent anti-Western stance, has been arrested in Paris, a source close to the case told AFP Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d792557e-8afa-11ef-b7b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1U53IC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d792557e-8afa-11ef-b7b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1U53IC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b9cb5c02-8aff-11ef-811f-005056a97652</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Oct 2024 14:17:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d792557e-8afa-11ef-b7b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1U53IC.jpg">© Stéphane de Sakutin, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France’s new health pass rules raise questions as many scramble to adapt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20210714-france-s-new-health-pass-rules-raise-questions-as-many-scramble-to-adapt</link><description>
While the extension of France’s health pass and other new anti-Covid 19 measures announced by President Emmanuel Macron Monday night are yet to be hammered out in detail, what’s certain is that a full-throttled return to a normal life of frequenting café terraces, restaurants, cinemas, theatres and other culture and leisure activities will now hinge on having a pass sanitaire (or health pass).
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95a7a1f4-e018-11eb-931e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/61be21e7dd8409eb6f2604b7d2e8d59f8e2865dc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95a7a1f4-e018-11eb-931e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/61be21e7dd8409eb6f2604b7d2e8d59f8e2865dc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5823e86e-e4b0-11eb-8c07-005056bf762b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Jul 2021 16:03:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95a7a1f4-e018-11eb-931e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/61be21e7dd8409eb6f2604b7d2e8d59f8e2865dc.jpg">© Sameer Al-Doumy, AFP</source><dc:creator>Romain BRUNET</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Daughter loses legal case in bitter Asterix family feud</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/20131211-daughter-loses-legal-case-bitter-asterix-family-feud-france-comics</link><description>A long-running family feud between Asterix co-creator Albert Uderzo and his daughter took a new twist on Tuesday after judges dismissed a claim by Sylvie Uderzo that her father was mentally frail and being exploited.</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abe23e78-093f-11e9-b87e-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/asterix_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abe23e78-093f-11e9-b87e-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/asterix_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">563894c2-cafc-11e7-8241-005056bf73c0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Dec 2013 18:09:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abe23e78-093f-11e9-b87e-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/asterix_0.jpg">Photo: AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Top contemporary French artist Christian Boltanski dies aged 76</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20210714-top-contemporary-french-artist-christian-boltanski-dies-aged-76</link><description>
Christian Boltanski, one of France's top contemporary artists whose multimedia works probed the meaning of mortality and memory, has died aged 76, a former museum director told AFP on Sunday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bb5a986-e4b7-11eb-b34d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/e857c10696aa723e38930cb9e30ea78aa32eb150.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bb5a986-e4b7-11eb-b34d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/e857c10696aa723e38930cb9e30ea78aa32eb150.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b7135ce8-e4c8-11eb-89be-005056bf762b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Jul 2021 18:44:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bb5a986-e4b7-11eb-b34d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/e857c10696aa723e38930cb9e30ea78aa32eb150.jpg">© Miguel Riopa, AFP</source><dc:creator>NEWS WIRES</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's top court blocks Macron's social media ban for under-15s</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260814-france-s-constitutional-authority-strikes-down-social-media-ban-for-under-15s</link><description>
France's constitutional council struck down a proposed ban on social media for children under 15 on Friday, citing freedom of expression. President Emmanuel Macron tasked Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu with re-working ​the draft legislation to take the Constitutional Council's concerns into account, the Elysée said in a statement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bd8eb1e-8005-11f1-836b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9J29ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bd8eb1e-8005-11f1-836b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9J29ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">593bbcd2-97e2-11f1-9b09-afe6d39a75d9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:17:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bd8eb1e-8005-11f1-836b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9J29ZQ.jpg">© Nicolas Tucat, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>In pictures: Wildfires ravage parts of southern France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260723-in-pictures-wildfires-ravage-parts-of-southern-france</link><description>
Thousands of people were evacuated in southwest France on Thursday, as a wildfire ravaged a seaside pine forest. Hundreds of firefighters were battling the fire, which started around midday on Wednesday. FRANCE 24 looks at some of the most striking images of the fire. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e23ac732-8688-11f1-9c16-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2VW6AU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e23ac732-8688-11f1-9c16-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2VW6AU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">356b841e-8689-11f1-a02b-a90349697956</guid><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 11:31:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e23ac732-8688-11f1-9c16-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2VW6AU.jpg">© Thibaud Moritz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>How the French army trains for 'high-intensity' combat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20210714-how-the-french-army-trains-for-high-intensity-conflict</link><description>
France's new military programming law increases the country's defence budget to 2 percent of GDP by 2025. It's an investment in the modernisation of equipment, but also in the training of soldiers. The aim is to teach soldiers to face an army at least as well equipped as that of France in a context of global rearmament. Our reporters Fadile Bhayat, Mandi Heshmati and Caroline Grandjean followed French troops during a "high-intensity" training exercise.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19df5ade-e4b0-11eb-b526-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Focus%2014%20juillet.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19df5ade-e4b0-11eb-b526-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Focus%2014%20juillet.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">023ce07e-e41d-11eb-a94a-005056bf762b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Jul 2021 14:42:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Fadile BHAYAT</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French police discover remains of five babies in a home in southeastern France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260728-french-police-discover-remains-of-five-babies-in-a-home-in-southeastern-france</link><description>
French police have opened a murder investigation after the remains of five newborns were discovered in cardboard boxes at a couple's home in southeastern France. The bodies were found after the woman's partner searched the flat following the home birth of a healthy baby, prompting hospital staff to alert prosecutors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5092e2a-8a89-11f1-b53d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3CP2LQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5092e2a-8a89-11f1-b53d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3CP2LQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1baf3ecc-8a89-11f1-a367-41ea8b95ada7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:48:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5092e2a-8a89-11f1-b53d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3CP2LQ.jpg">© Thibaud Moritz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'A lot of French politicians are out of touch with a large part of the population'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20220209-a-lot-of-french-politicians-are-out-of-touch-with-a-large-part-of-the-population</link><description>
Our guest is Fabien Truong, a sociologist, author and associate professor at the University of Paris. A former schoolteacher, he spent a decade following the lives of around 20 of his students, charting their progress from the time they took their end of school exams to when they finished their higher education. Those 10 years took in the riots that rocked France back in 2005 to the terror attacks of January 2015. He gives us his take on the French presidential election campaign, as seen from the suburbs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a29e27fe-89a3-11ec-8742-005056a90321/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13035161446203b32c2451f2.07563475.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a29e27fe-89a3-11ec-8742-005056a90321/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13035161446203b32c2451f2.07563475.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2534ffb8-8980-11ec-8ce4-005056a97652</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Feb 2022 12:31:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Thousands of tourists forced to evacuate as fire rages in southwest France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260723-thousands-of-tourists-forced-to-evacuate-as-fire-rages-in-southwest-france</link><description>
More than 20,000 people, most of them tourists, on Thursday were evacuated as a wildfire ravaged a forest in Le Porge, southwest France. The fire started midday on Wednesday and hundreds of firefighters have been deployed to the region. France has experienced three heatwaves since May, fuelling wildfires. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7522e0a-866f-11f1-93f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2XC3E8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7522e0a-866f-11f1-93f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2XC3E8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3e818896-8670-11f1-8d96-8b91e7fe4f70</guid><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 08:49:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7522e0a-866f-11f1-93f1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2XC3E8.jpg">© Romain Perrocheau, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>'Tefal campaign': with Covid-19 monopolising voters' minds, nothing sticks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20220209-tefal-campaign-pandemic-prudent-president-keep-french-election-race-on-the-backburner</link><description>
Presidential campaigns offer an abundance of catch phrases, whether slogans finessed by a candidate's team to deliver maximum impact or coined spontaneously on the trail. The proclamations – and gaffes – of presidential hopefuls bring texture to an election race and come to define a campaign, whether for a news cycle or forever in the history books. FRANCE 24 brings you the buzzwords of the 2022 French presidential race. In the spotlight: "Tefal campaign".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2debad06-88f3-11ec-b463-005056a90321/w:1024/p:16x9/1280x720-Tefa-campaign.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2debad06-88f3-11ec-b463-005056a90321/w:1024/p:16x9/1280x720-Tefa-campaign.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4e47fa4-88f4-11ec-97bf-005056a97652</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Feb 2022 10:43:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2debad06-88f3-11ec-b463-005056a90321/w:1024/p:16x9/1280x720-Tefa-campaign.png">© FMM Graphic Studio</source><dc:creator>Tracy MCNICOLL</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French environment minister to stay in post amid 'urgency' to act on climate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260722-french-environment-minister-announces-plan-to-resign-over-approved-pesticide-bill</link><description>
France's environment minister Monique Barbut said Wednesday that she will remain in her post despite her disagreement with a bill on bee-harming pesticides, given the "urgency" to act on climate change. Earlier in the day, Barbut said she would submit her resignation to the president. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4b1965c-85a2-11f1-a8e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-03T000000Z-2124378622-MT1ABCPR1008413045-RTRMADP-3-ABACA-PRESS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4b1965c-85a2-11f1-a8e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-03T000000Z-2124378622-MT1ABCPR1008413045-RTRMADP-3-ABACA-PRESS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3fb6548-85a5-11f1-84de-c1013e91da27</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 08:22:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4b1965c-85a2-11f1-a8e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-03T000000Z-2124378622-MT1ABCPR1008413045-RTRMADP-3-ABACA-PRESS.jpg">© Jumeau Alexis, ABACA via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Louvre gallery where jewellery heist took place to reopen to public</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260722-louvre-gallery-where-jewellery-heist-took-place-to-reopen-to-public</link><description>
The Apollo Gallery at Paris's Louvre Museum, the site of the jewelry heist of October 2025, is set to reopen to the public on Wednesday without any jewelry on display.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c320d7dc-7d3d-11f1-bfeb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26056440917372.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c320d7dc-7d3d-11f1-bfeb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26056440917372.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">daed1298-8596-11f1-9cfd-a37c7f360e9d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 06:58:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c320d7dc-7d3d-11f1-bfeb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26056440917372.jpg">© Thomas Padilla, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France 2022: The Choice</category><title>Battle for the French far right: Zemmour, Le Pen try to steal each other's thunder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-2022-the-campaign/20220207-battle-for-the-far-right-zemmour-le-pen-fight-to-steal-each-other-s-thunder</link><description>
As France's April presidential election approaches, the campaign is getting under way in earnest. In this edition of our new show, we focus on the French Communist Party attempting a political comeback and discuss at length the battle raging between Eric Zemmour and Marine Le Pen for leadership of the French far right. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b99fd93a-885d-11ec-9917-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/XX%20NW%20OOV%20SPLIT%20LE%20PEN%20ZEMMOUR.transfer001.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b99fd93a-885d-11ec-9917-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/XX%20NW%20OOV%20SPLIT%20LE%20PEN%20ZEMMOUR.transfer001.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ecf0724-8861-11ec-862b-005056bf762b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Feb 2022 22:00:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's National Rally targeted as part of Europe-wide raids over alleged far-right embezzlement</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260630-police-raid-eu-far-right-offices-including-s-france-s-national-rally-over-allegations-of-misuse-of-eu-funds</link><description>
France's National Rally was on Tuesday targeted as part of Europe-wide raids following suspicions of the misappropriation of European funds by the now-defunct Identity and Democracy (ID) group of MEPs, the European Public Prosecutor’s Office (EPPO) said, onfirming a report in French daily Le Monde.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02cf78a6-74ac-11f1-8b8c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7NE7PP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02cf78a6-74ac-11f1-8b8c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7NE7PP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b87222c6-74ac-11f1-a3cc-3b7ac5941c54</guid><pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 17:54:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02cf78a6-74ac-11f1-8b8c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7NE7PP.jpg">© Wojtek Radwanski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France explored Pegasus spyware deal despite Morocco espionage claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260716-france-explored-pegasus-spyware-deal-despite-morocco-espionage-claims</link><description>
France briefly explored acquiring the controversial Pegasus spyware in 2019, according to media investigations, even as Morocco was allegedly using the Israeli-made surveillance tool to target French ministers. The report claims President Emmanuel Macron ultimately rejected the purchase to avoid reliance on foreign technology. Morocco has denied the spying allegations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/67849330-8113-11f1-8cfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22233489166213.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/67849330-8113-11f1-8cfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22233489166213.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29c82bac-8112-11f1-8f78-1f5f45bd9f1e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 12:45:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/67849330-8113-11f1-8cfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22233489166213.jpg">© Sebastian Scheiner, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron vows to replant Fontainebleau forest after devastating wildfires</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260716-macron-vows-to-replant-fontainebleau-forest-after-devastating-wildfires</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday vowed to replant Fontainebleau forest after devastating wildfires blazed through at least 10% of the 20,000 hectare demain and forced hundreds of residents to flee. The historic forest, just south of Paris, draws hikers, climbers and nature lovers from all over the world every year. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d85e184-810b-11f1-831c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26197353090488.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d85e184-810b-11f1-831c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26197353090488.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64fcb732-810e-11f1-bb97-7d2627b8f363</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 12:05:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d85e184-810b-11f1-831c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26197353090488.jpg">© Mohammed Badra, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France records 300 excess deaths during unseasonal May heatwave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260630-france-records-300-excess-deaths-during-unseasonal-may-heatwave</link><description>
A five-day heatwave in May caused at least 300 more deaths than expected across France, health officials said Tuesday. The unseasonal heatwave was followed in June by 11 days of the hottest temperatures the country has experienced since records began. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0192ae3e-748b-11f1-b7b7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-27T085518Z-634352096-RC22XLAONE7P-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HOTELS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0192ae3e-748b-11f1-b7b7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-27T085518Z-634352096-RC22XLAONE7P-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HOTELS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e775446c-748a-11f1-9e69-ffae464c345d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 14:05:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0192ae3e-748b-11f1-b7b7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-27T085518Z-634352096-RC22XLAONE7P-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HOTELS.jpg">© Alice Sacco, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>‘Like working in a kettle’: France’s overcrowded prisons swelter under historic heatwave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260625-like-working-in-a-kettle-france-s-overcrowded-prisons-swelter-under-historic-heatwave</link><description>
The deadly heatwave sweeping France has once again exposed the structural problems of the country’s chronically overcrowded prisons, with groups of three or four detainees crammed into airless cells built to hold a lone prisoner. Analysts and prison staff alike have criticised a penal system that continues to see mass incarceration as the main means of cracking down on crime.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3725d5f2-70ae-11f1-80b6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92XP8G3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3725d5f2-70ae-11f1-80b6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92XP8G3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3e1dc5e-70ab-11f1-86ea-a5748fcbbc4b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 16:57:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3725d5f2-70ae-11f1-80b6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92XP8G3.jpg">© Stéphane de Sakutin, AFP</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France ponders failure to protect children as school abuse scandal rocks Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260521-france-failure-protect-children-school-abuse-scandal-rocks-paris-gregoire</link><description>
Paris Mayor Emmanuel Grégoire has acknowledged “systemic” failings as investigators probe allegations of child abuse by non-teaching staff at more than 100 nurseries and primary schools in the French capital. The scandal has shocked the public and exposed major shortfalls in child protection and accountability.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88540c5a-51fa-11f1-af76-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/5db0fa52c36b482fc039d288515bcd84f6bb828f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88540c5a-51fa-11f1-af76-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/5db0fa52c36b482fc039d288515bcd84f6bb828f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aedf5382-54f4-11f1-85a7-df27a4f2ab30</guid><pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 09:34:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88540c5a-51fa-11f1-af76-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/5db0fa52c36b482fc039d288515bcd84f6bb828f.jpg">© Martin Bureau, AFP file photo</source><dc:creator>Benjamin DODMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>France in focus</category><title>The rooftops of Paris with the zinc craftsmen of the sky</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20241014-the-rooftops-of-paris-with-the-zinc-craftsmen-of-the-sky</link><description>
Paris’s slate-grey zinc rooftops are a key part of the French capital’s visual identity. They have long inspired painters and filmmakers and only exist thanks to the expertise of the roofers who install and maintain the galvanised metal covering many of Paris’s buildings. Their expertise could soon be included in UNESCO's intangible heritage list, as the profession adapts to the challenges of global warming. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c607e114-8a11-11ef-9e1a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Photo%20toits%20de%20Paris.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c607e114-8a11-11ef-9e1a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Photo%20toits%20de%20Paris.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8962130-8a21-11ef-85ac-005056bf1351</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Oct 2024 12:51:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Olivia SALAZAR WINSPEAR</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's top health advisory body wants compulsory vaccinations for health workers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20210710-france-s-top-health-advisory-body-wants-compulsory-vaccinations-for-health-workers</link><description>
