In Paris, parents are now dropping their children off at school in a climate of anxiety. For several months, reports of physical and sexual abuse involving nursery school children have been mounting. These cases are said to have taken place during after-school care and lunch breaks, when the children are supervised by non-teaching staff. In 2026 alone, 78 youth workers were suspended in Paris, 31 of them on suspicion of sexual abuse. Warning: viewers may find this report disturbing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3688ce90-43c9-11f1-8bd7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/periscolaire.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3688ce90-43c9-11f1-8bd7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/periscolaire.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb342f66-43ca-11f1-88cf-97fcecc873a1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 13:58:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Noémie ROCHE</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French navy boards Russia-linked tanker in Mediterranean</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260320-french-navy-seizes-oil-tanker-sailing-from-russia-accused-of-flying-false-flag-in-mediterranean</link><description>
